Notes:
- cluster_sum matches the convention in ../raw-io/peak_aggregate_summary.py
  (sum of per-process bandwidths). Overestimates when nodes finish at
  different times.
- conservative is the honest wall-clock aggregate. If it is well below
  cluster_sum, tasks did not overlap enough — for seq_* this is
  expected at small sizes (short single-pass runtime).
- seq_* runs are single-pass (loops=1) with nrfiles chosen so per-job
  working set = TOTAL_PER_JOB. Client cache is bypassed via direct=1 +
  invalidate=1 + fadvise_hint=1. Server CBOX cache is mitigated by
  cluster-aggregate working set > cache size, not flushed.
